{
  "name": "a typo fix in a huge repo scores zero, not eighteen",
  "description": "THE regression test for ADR-0007 §1. Before disqualification existed, a README typo in a 40,000-star repository scored ~18, because project reach is a property of the repository rather than the change — outscoring a careful fix in a small library. The verdict must bypass the arithmetic entirely, not reduce it.\n\nIt also proves the consequence in ADR-0007 §3: the rejected PR does not count toward standing, so Go sits at FOUR surviving PRs and stays secondary — unranked, despite the claim carrying five.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories"],
